      "repeat": "cohorts",
      "rows": [
        "COHORT",
        "SCENE",
        {
          "repeat": "metrics",
          "rows": [
            "SCOPE"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "REPORT_COST",
    "END"
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Measurement-only on50; no performance adoption from observer frame rates.",
    "One-in16 eligible attempts sampled independently per cohort. Aggregate raw counts/ticks first; unused means null.",
    "Inclusive scopes overlap. Exclusive subtracts measured direct children but includes observer/unmeasured work, not pure CPU/GPU cost.",
    "State only at original Main.Draw boundaries: no guarantee of intermediate toggle-and-return, current effective render camera/zoom or arbitrary capture modes.",
    "Player is raw Main.player[myPlayer]; camera Main.screenPosition; zoom raw GameZoomTarget; ui_scale raw get_UIScale; mouse positions are boundary Main fields. Hover/mouse item null encoded-1, not game strings.",
    "world excludes paused; inventory and inventory_paused are separate. Dead/ghost/spectator/menu/map/invalid frames excluded from costs and explicitly counted.",
    "Scene ranges cover all eligible cohort boundary snapshots, not only timed samples; sample count twice cohort frames.",
    "Layer false returns are legitimate stops, separately counted; incomplete/failed scopes do not donate valid sample timing.",
    "Snapshots and clock pairs are reported overhead indicators, not automatic deductions. Reports measure body before footer; report cooldown anchors later without claiming post-END clock validity.",
    "Any measurement_invalid flag blocks performance interpretation. Structurally malformed/partial packets rejected, never silently dropped."
  ]
}
